<.shell current={:icons}>
  <h1>Icons</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Lucide's outline icons, with 1.5px lines at every size. An icon helps people find
    or recognize something, and never replaces the words.
  </p>

  <h2>The set</h2>
  <p>
    Every icon the app uses, with its use. Each is a file in <code>assets/icons</code>, and a test fails until it is on this list.
  </p>
  <.table id="icon-set" rows={icons()}>
    <:col :let={{name, _use}} label="16" class="w-px">
      <.icon name={name} size={:sm} />
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{name, _use}} label="20" class="w-px">
      <.icon name={name} />
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{name, _use}} label="24" class="w-px">
      <.icon name={name} size={:lg} />
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{name, _use}} label="Name" class="w-px mono whitespace-nowrap">
      {name}
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{_name, use}} label="Use">{use}</:col>
  </.table>

  <h2>Sizes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>16</strong>, <code>size=&lbrace;:sm&rbrace;</code>: beside sm text: breadcrumbs, back links, pagination, small buttons, chips.
    </li>
    <li><strong>20</strong>, the default: beside md text: buttons, banner titles, toasts.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>24</strong>, <code>size=&lbrace;:lg&rbrace;</code>: on its own line, such as warning text. A band draws it at 32.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In use</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <.form_actions>
      <.button href="#">
        Open in D4H <.icon name="external-link" size={:sm} />
      </.button>
      <.button icon="rotate-ccw-square">Rotate left</.button>
      <.button icon="rotate-cw-square">Rotate right</.button>
    </.form_actions>
  </div>

  <h2>Rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      An icon sits beside words. The only icon without words is the close or remove ×, and it has an <code>aria-label</code>.
    </li>
    <li>At most one icon per button. It leads, except the external-link icon, which trails.</li>
    <li>
      A button that says what it is doing while it waits takes its icon as <code>icon="…"</code>, and draws it itself: LiveView puts back only the text, so an
      icon inside it would go. The spinner takes the icon's place while it waits.
    </li>
    <li>
      A new icon comes from <a href="https://lucide.dev/icons/">Lucide</a>:
      <code>bin/icons add NAME</code>
      copies it into <code>assets/icons</code>, and it goes on this list. When none fits, draw one on Lucide's 24px grid with 2px lines, and say so on its first line, <code>&lt;!-- sd: what it is --&gt;</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>bin/icons check</code>
      lists the icons Lucide has changed since we copied them. The monthly dependency review runs it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Only the uses listed above. No icons beside headings, in table cells, or for decoration.
    </li>
    <li>Icons take the text colour. Banners and toasts colour theirs to match.</li>
    <li>
      In the app: <code>&lt;.icon name="chevron-left" size=&lbrace;:sm&rbrace; /&gt;</code>. A name with no file in
      <code>assets/icons</code>
      fails to compile.
    </li>
  </ul>
</.shell>
